      "Torghatten is a mountain with a hole straight through it, big enough to walk through. The story goes that a troll fired an arrow at a girl he fancied, a king threw his hat in the way, and the hat turned to stone with the arrow through it. The geologists have a different explanation. It's less fun.",
      "You walk into the hole. Wind comes with you, then a lot more wind, and then Gale, spinning through the gap like it was built for the purpose.",
      "Inside a mountain there's nowhere to be blown to. Gale howls and shoves and gets nowhere, because the frost has your boots stuck fast and you've stopped trying to move. You just hold your rows and hit back.",
